  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New Jersey federal contract obligations totaled $68.5M in FY2027 to date. The federal government issued 418 awards in the state and the average award size was $164K. New Jersey federal contract obligations fell 99.3% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations at $53.7M. CELLCO PARTNERSHIP was the single largest vendor, receiving $31.4M, and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) was the largest NAICS industry with $28.3M in obligations. The FY22 to FY26 historical series shows multi-year obligations near $9.2B to $9.8B, and FY27 to date stands apart at $68.5M. These figures are fiscal year to date totals and represent contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 to date versus prior years?",
        "body": "New Jersey federal contract obligations fell 99.3% year over year. FY27 to date obligations are $68.5M compared with prior fiscal years that ranged from $9.2B to $9.8B. The award count in FY27 to date is 418 and the average award size is $164K. This fiscal year to date snapshot is a partial total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are FY2027 to date obligations concentrated in New Jersey?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $53.7M, the largest buying agency in FY2027 to date. CELLCO PARTNERSHIP received $31.4M and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) received $28.3M, which are the largest vendor and industry concentrations respectively. Other sizable agency obligations include the Department of Justice at $8.3M and the Department of Agriculture at $3M."
      }
    ]
  },
